---
// Second Thought — projekt központi oldal (hub), /projects/second-thought
//
// Szerepe: rövid tájékozódási pont — mi ez, demó, aloldalak, linkek.
// A részletek az .md aloldalakon: src/content/projects/second-thought/*.md
// Új aloldal = új .md `project: "second-thought"` mezővel → itt magától megjelenik, `order` szerint.
//
// A TODO-dobozok csak vázat jelölnek, élesítés előtt mind tűnjön el.
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectSection from "../../../components/ProjectSection.astro";
import ProjectTile from "../../../components/ProjectTile.astro";
import YouTubeFacade from "../../../components/YouTubeFacade.astro";
import createSlug from "../../../lib/createSlug";

const PROJECT = "second-thought";
const REPO_URL = "https://github.com/asukix/second-thought";
const README_URL = `${REPO_URL}#readme`;

const subpages = (await getCollection("projects"))
  .filter((e) => e.data.project === PROJECT)
  .filter((e) => import.meta.env.DEV || !e.data.draft)
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);

// Kapcsolódó cikkek: az AI taggel jelölt deep bitek, legfrissebb elöl.
// Új AI-s bit magától bekerül; a többi a tag-oldalon („More”).
const RELATED_TAG = "AI";
const RELATED_LIMIT = 2;
const relatedBits = (await getCollection("deep-bits"))
  .filter((b) => !b.data.draft && b.data.tags?.includes(RELATED_TAG))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
---

<BaseLayout title="Second Thought" sideBarActiveItemID="projects" favicon="/projects/second-thought/logo-dark.svg">
  <!-- TODO: description prop a BaseLayoutnak (SEO / megosztási előnézet) -->

  <header class="mb-8">
    <!-- Logó (világos változat) a cím előtt; a sötét változat a favicon -->
    <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-3">
      <img src="/projects/second-thought/logo-light.svg" width="56" height="56" alt="" class="w-14 h-14 shrink-0" />
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Second Thought</h1>
    </div>
    <ProjectSection as="div">
      <p>My website is a space for thinking. It contains thinking content alongside the usual articles.</p>
      <p><b>Second Thought</b> is a tool that helps me do it better. The tool is my article harness around the LLM.</p>
    </ProjectSection>
    <div class="flex gap-3 mt-4">
      <a href={REPO_URL} target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline">GitHub</a>
      <a href={README_URL} target="_blank" class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost">README</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <ProjectSection title="What is Second Thought?">
    <p>Second Thought is a tool that helps me to check my articles and improve their quality.</p>
    <p>It currently has two main features:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Language check:</b> helps to correct grammar.</li>
      <li><b>Editorial review:</b> provides feedback about the article's content and structure.</li>
    </ul>
  </ProjectSection>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────
       2. DEMO
       YouTube video
       ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <YouTubeFacade
      id="BwX59-gC_18"
      title="Second Thought demo"
      thumbnail="/projects/second-thought/youtube-thumbnail.png"
    />
  </section>

  <ProjectSection title="Why did I want my own harness?">
    <p>Firstly, I was learning about AI, LLMs and harnesses. I wanted to create my own harness and try it myself.</p>
    <p>Secondly, I wanted a tool that only provides information and tips for me.</p>
  </ProjectSection>

  <ProjectSection title="Harness of Second Thought vs. a general agent">
    <p>In the diagram below, you can see the structure of Second Thought's harness compared to a general agent.</p>
    <p>You can see that the input is an article that is first segmented, then processed by the harness. 
      After that, the context is passed to the LLM. The process doesn't stop here. 
      The output of the LLM is then processed by a second harness layer (guard, diff).
      When the LLM provides the output, the harness can check the output, handle errors and provide feedback to the user.
    </p>
    <p><br/>
      <a
        href="/projects/second-thought/Harness.webp"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        class="block cursor-zoom-in"
        title="Open full-size image"
      >
        <img
          src="/projects/second-thought/Harness.webp"
          width="1251"
          height="1002"
          loading="lazy"
          alt="Side-by-side diagram. Left: a general agent, where the harness (system prompt, tools, context history) builds the context, the LLM's output goes straight to the user, and the context loops back into the history. Right: Second Thought, where the article is first segmented, the harness builds the context without tools or a loop, and after the LLM a second harness layer (guard, diff) produces the output."
          class="w-full h-auto rounded-lg"
        />
      </a>
    </p>
  </ProjectSection>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────
       5. NYITOTT HELYEK — döntés kell, hova kerülnek
       • Mit tanultam + How it was built (Claude co-author):
           itt a hubon szekcióként, VAGY saját aloldal (új .md, `order`).
       • Kulcsdöntések és trade-offok:
           szétosztva az aloldalakon, ahol keletkeztek, VAGY külön döntésnapló aloldal.
       • Korlátok és következő lépések: nem itt — link a README Roadmapjére (lent).
       ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <ProjectSection title="What I learned during the project">
    <ul>
      <li>Stop and give time to thinking</li>
      <li>Quality over features</li>
      <li>Work with AI trade-offs</li>
      <li>Architecture before implementation</li>
    </ul>
    <p><a href="/projects/second-thought/lessons" class="link link-hover">Read more →</a></p>
  </ProjectSection>

  <ProjectSection title="Subpages">
    <section class="mb-10 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      {
        subpages.map((page) => (
          <ProjectTile
            href={`/projects/${page.slug}`}
            title={page.data.title}
            description={page.data.description}
            badge={page.data.draft ? "draft" : undefined}
          />
        ))
      }
    </section>
  </ProjectSection>
  
  <ProjectSection title="Connected articles">
    <section class="mb-10">      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {
          relatedBits.slice(0, RELATED_LIMIT).map((bit) => (
            <ProjectTile
              href={`/deep-bits/${createSlug(bit.data.title, bit.slug)}`}
              title={bit.data.title}
              description={bit.data.description}
            />
          ))
        }
      </div>
      {
        relatedBits.length > RELATED_LIMIT && (
          <a href={`/deep-bits/tag/${RELATED_TAG}`} class="link link-hover text-sm inline-block mt-4">
            More ({relatedBits.length - RELATED_LIMIT}) →
          </a>
        )
      }
    </section>
  </ProjectSection>

  <!-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────
       6. LINKBLOKK
       Repó, README (roadmap ott él).
       ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <footer class="mb-10">
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <ul class="list-none space-y-1 text-sm">
      <li><a href={REPO_URL} target="_blank" class="link link-hover">GitHub repository</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${REPO_URL}#roadmap`} target="_blank" class="link link-hover">Roadmap (README)</a></li>
    </ul>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Vázjelölő — élesítés előtt minden .todo elem eltűnik */
  .todo {
    border: 1px dashed oklch(var(--bc) / 0.3);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .todo-tall {
    min-height: 12rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }
</style>
